.TH HSH 1 "April 2026" "1.0" "Simple Shell Manual"

.SH NAME
hsh \- simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsh
[\fIcommand_file\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple UNIX shell that reads and executes commands from standard
input or a file.
It mimics the behavior of
.BR /bin/sh
and supports both interactive and non-interactive modes.

In interactive mode, the shell displays a prompt
.B ($)
and waits for the user to type a command.

In non-interactive mode, the shell reads commands from a pipe or a
file without displaying a prompt.

.SH INVOCATION
If no argument is given,
.B hsh
runs in interactive mode and displays a prompt.
If a command file is piped or redirected to standard input,
.B hsh
runs in non-interactive mode.

.SH COMMANDS
Each command is a sequence of words separated by spaces or tabs.
The first word is the command name. Remaining words are passed as
arguments.

.B hsh
searches for the command in the directories listed in the
.B PATH
environment variable.
If the command contains a slash, it is used directly as a path.

.SH BUILT-INS

.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell. The exit status is 0.

.TP
.B env
Print the current environment variables, one per line, in the format
.I NAME=value.

.SH PATH RESOLUTION
When a command has no slash, the shell searches each directory in
.B PATH
in order.
For each directory, it checks if an executable file with the command
name exists using
.BR access (2).

.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of
.B hsh
is the exit status of the last command executed.
If a command is not found, the exit status is
.BR 127 .
